{
  "id": "anomaly-cold-halo",
  "title": "Anomaly - the cold halo",
  "notes": [
    "ION anomaly. Deliberately NOT a violet wash: earlier review threw that out and the profile",
    "still says so. What replaces it is a single large STRUCTURE - the far shell of an old blast,",
    "two arcs at different radii and sweeps so the shell reads as a curved surface with thickness",
    "rather than a drawn ring, plus one dense knot where the shell piles up brightest.",
    "The arcs use the same plateau-plus-erosion construction as the other plates, so the shell is",
    "torn and lit rather than a smooth band, and both ends dissolve through the taper instead of",
    "stopping on a shared cut-off.",
    "The right half carries a second protected void because the anomaly profile spawns a live",
    "wormhole there and the sky must not compete with it. Corridor void as everywhere else."
  ],
